#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/commit.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "`commit.cleanup`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/commit.adoc:16
msgid ""
"This setting overrides the default of the `--cleanup` option in `git "
"commit`. {see-git-commit} Changing the default can be useful when you always "
"want to keep lines that begin with the comment character "
"(`core.commentChar`, default `#`)  in your log message, in which case you "
"would do `git config commit.cleanup whitespace` (note that you will have to "
"remove the help lines that begin with the comment character in the commit "
"log template yourself, if you do this)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/commit.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "`commit.gpgSign`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/commit.adoc:23
msgid ""
"A boolean to specify whether all commits should be GPG signed.  Use of this "
"option when doing operations such as rebase can result in a large number of "
"commits being signed. It may be convenient to use an agent to avoid typing "
"your GPG passphrase several times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/commit.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "`commit.status`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/commit.adoc:28
msgid ""
"A boolean to enable/disable inclusion of status information in the commit "
"message template when using an editor to prepare the commit message.  "
"Defaults to `true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/commit.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "`commit.template`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/commit.adoc:32
msgid ""
"Specify the pathname of a file to use as the template for new commit "
"messages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/commit.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "`commit.verbose`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/config/commit.adoc:35
msgid ""
"A boolean or int to specify the level of verbosity with `git commit`.  "
"{see-git-commit}"
msgstr ""
